  "summary": "Multi Discipline Engineering & Facility Manager\nManage the worlds largest, NASA recognized, Rendezvous, Proximity Operations and Docking (RPOD) risk reduction testing center. Lead a specialized team of engineers to perform high visibility projects on aggressive schedules. Provide exceptional customer service to our testing clients and their customers, ensuring they have the right resources and support to complete their tests. Work closely with program management to ensure the delivery of the desired message to high ranking NASA and military personnel through effective demonstrations of capability, tours, and hosting events. Successfully coach, mentor, and guide the development of team members. Advocate for the team, manage customer expectations, and navigate difficult conversations. \n\nPrevious Experience: FPGA/HW Lead Engineer/Systems Engineer\nProposal writing, created recourse/budget loaded schedules, project management, personnel management, trainer, mentor, LM Recruiter(7 years), excellent presenter, tour guide\nFPGA development (Xilinx, ISE, Vivado, high speed), board design (Zuken), embedded software design, simulator architect/design/build/maintenance (10M Simulator)\n",
